WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.332 --> 00:00:07.243
Offer Check tells you if a job offer really beats what you have now. Here's the order to fill it in.

2
00:00:07.615 --> 00:00:09.810
Step one: your current package, top to bottom.

3
00:00:10.508 --> 00:00:13.903
Base salary, employer pension, and typical bonus.

4
00:00:14.578 --> 00:00:16.664
How much of that bonus you can rely on.

5
00:00:17.295 --> 00:00:19.881
Then allowances, medical, and holiday.

6
00:00:20.352 --> 00:00:23.266
Finally, your commute: cost and hours.

7
00:00:23.927 --> 00:00:28.490
Step two: ask the recruiter these questions, and note the answers.

8
00:00:29.173 --> 00:00:31.689
Get their salary band before you name a number.

9
00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:38.057
Step three: fill in the offer, in the same order. Base, pension and bonus.

10
00:00:38.623 --> 00:00:41.680
If the bonus is only a target, count half of it.

11
00:00:42.128 --> 00:00:45.504
Then allowances, medical, holiday and commute.

12
00:00:46.314 --> 00:00:53.949
Step four: set your decision lines. 10% and 20% are good defaults. Raise them for riskier roles.

13
00:00:54.861 --> 00:01:00.786
The verdict: break-even. Only eight percent better, once pension and bonus are counted.

14
00:01:01.288 --> 00:01:05.828
And the base salary to ask for: about £83,400.

15
00:01:06.651 --> 00:01:10.141
Offer Check. Know your numbers before you say yes.

